7. SET pseudo-operation:==============

   - 'SET' assigns the specified value directly to the label on that line instead of the current PC.
   - Emits no code and does not advance the address counter.
   - Forward references (label used before SET definition) and backward references work seamlessly across passes.
   - Verified in `tests/test03.asm` and `tests/test03.log`.
   - Placement rule: the emulator reads memory straight from address 0 and knows nothing of `SET`/`data`, so number lines must sit after `HALT` (numbers at the end). A number in the walking path is read as an order (a `SET 75` word fails as unknown opcode 75). Programmers must write code this way; an earlier try where `SET` took no address was dropped to keep our `test3.o` byte-equal to the sample.

